{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere","id":1508768,"title":"Tome of the Pentacle-The Tremere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-18T12:11:46-07:00","id":1508768,"title":"Tome of the Pentacle-The Tremere","content":"Before they were jackals on the edge of magical societes and deep well of prices paid, They were the the Fames Draconis, the Hunger of the Dragon, and the sixth Order of the Diamond. <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/tome-of-the-pentacle-tremere/\" target=\"_blank\">This is their story.</a> Talk about it here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T12:26:06-07:00","id":1508769,"title":"","content":"I find it very amusing that the Begotten and the Created both get leniency from the Tremere. I guess you can\u2019t eat what isn\u2019t there, and nobody eats divine fire for real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T12:38:19-07:00","id":1508770,"title":"","content":"Heh, nobody likes spicy foods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T13:41:06-07:00","id":1508771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508769#post1508769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it very amusing that the Begotten and the Created both get leniency from the Tremere. I guess you can\u2019t eat what isn\u2019t there, and nobody eats divine fire for real.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have more thoughts on this for later, but as a short hand-Beasts are nothing <i>but</i> soul stuff, and the Prometheans are trying to transmute their selves into having a soul, where most other entities in the world can be described as having damaged or polluted soul stuff that's needs to be down by the Final Watchtower.<br /> <br /> I was more surprised that I was equally surprised that Beasts got an exemption, and I'll go into why when I have time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T13:43:36-07:00","id":1508772,"title":"","content":"Fun seeing the tie back to the shenanigans of the Sundered World in the lore there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T13:51:08-07:00","id":1508775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508771#post1508771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have more thoughts on this for later, but as a short hand-Beasts are nothing <i>but</i> soul stuff, and the Prometheans are trying to transmute their selves into having a soul, where most other entities in the world can be described as having damaged or polluted soul stuff that's needs to be down by the Final Watchtower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, Right, they have a portion of the Sea of Souls acting as a soul, instead of an individual soul. They have all souls as their soul\u2026kinda.<br /> <br /> I actually assumed the Remade would be on the list of do not touch, but as you point out, damaged souls are fine to down. So where does that leave Sin-Eaters? Technically they are hypothetically living ghost with an another more chthonic ghost as its soul, right? Are they on the pile of do not touch? Or are they another abomination to down?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-18-2023, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T14:25:13-07:00","id":1508778,"title":"","content":"it's almost refreshing,mages that glorify their hunger for power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T14:53:44-07:00","id":1508780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508772#post1508772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun seeing the tie back to the shenanigans of the Sundered World in the lore there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has been awhile for me; could you spell it out please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T14:56:07-07:00","id":1508781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508771#post1508771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have more thoughts on this for later, but as a short hand-Beasts are nothing <i>but</i> soul stuff, and the Prometheans are trying to transmute their selves into having a soul, where most other entities in the world can be described as having damaged or polluted soul stuff that's needs to be down by the Final Watchtower.<br /> <br /> I was more surprised that I was equally surprised that Beasts got an exemption, and I'll go into why when I have time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere seem to be almost mage-beasts of a sort.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T15:02:37-07:00","id":1508782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508780#post1508780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It has been awhile for me; could you spell it out please?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> The Sundered Worlds' big plot on the Mage side was the murder of several Pangaeans and the removal of their Hearts/Omphalos Stones, which were like uber soul stones. The Tremere include this as their starting place for the study of Souls as Power/The Subjugation of Gods/Hunger. Really cool stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T16:57:46-07:00","id":1508793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508780#post1508780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has been awhile for me; could you spell it out please?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;[The Suspire] recounts their mythic history, claiming a connection to prehistoric mages capable of stealing souls from powerful primordial entities and exploiting them to power their Demesnes&quot; is almost certainly a reference to the chronologically earliest Dark Era from Dark Eras 1, where the dirty little Lie about the &quot;gifts from the gods&quot; serving as the core of the powerful Demesnes at the heart of many ancient Vinca communities is that mages sought out divinity made flesh and tore the stone soul from its chest when it would not give its patronage willingly, and they kept doing this despite the first such act ruining a swath of the Border Marches and despite omphalos stones being huge \u2014 the pieces of them used to form Demesnes are twice as tall as a person.<br /> <br /> Pangaeans possessed Arcana and the ability to meditate themselves bodily into the Astral Realms on either side of the Omphalos, and Demesnes made with a piece of their soul are not subject to Dissonance and provide easier exceptional success to spells cast with their Arcana, so you can see the throughline from there to the Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T19:29:36-07:00","id":1508807,"title":"","content":"Oh my. This is a treat. <br /> <br /> And it does look like that <b>hunger</b> defines a significant portion of the supernatural world, indeed\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T22:44:16-07:00","id":1508838,"title":"","content":"Eh, aside from a few interesting facts there is nothing we didn't know from N&amp;A. What a shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T00:40:27-07:00","id":1508857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508772#post1508772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun seeing the tie back to the shenanigans of the Sundered World in the lore there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I enjoyed that as well.<br /> <br /> I will admit, this elaboration of a historical foundation for their organisation does make the use of a Latin name more curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T02:16:59-07:00","id":1508869,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11880_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11880\" data-vbnamecard=\"11880\">Dark Archon</a>. It's well written and compelling, <i>but</i> to me it doesn't feel meaningfully different enough to their appearance in N&amp;A.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T07:25:58-07:00","id":1508885,"title":"","content":"I personally find it very worthwhile to see the perspective on what they sell their philosophy as when becoming Hollow isn't a basic point of initiation and when they have to fit into the Diamond sect, which is defined by the fact that each Order is seen as a component of an idealised magical society. That latter one was actually a notable sticking point for me, and I feel as though this write-up does make the reconciliation fairly central (including with acknowledgement that it's not exactly a smooth fit).<br /> <br /> Plus, it might have to write from the perspective of not assuming everybody reading has access to Nameless and Accursed. Tome of the Pentacle is about the history of the Orders, so the entire exiled Diamond Order has to be significant in that context in its own right, even if it turns out that the philosophy is recognisable to the modern version (that has no qualms about describing itself as part of Atlantis).<br /> <br /> Still and all, it does seem to suggest that Arc had a point about this not being the most novel preview for people to clamour for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T08:28:22-07:00","id":1508893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508885#post1508885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, it might have to write from the perspective of not assuming everybody reading has access to Nameless and Accursed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. Although it raises the question that it's still a rewrite, it <i>is</i> different. Are we meant to take away that the Tremere have meaningfully changed?<br /> <br /> Like, their magical symbolism here is 'Hunger', whilst their modern counterpart is 'The Ephemeral &amp; Physical are One'. There's crossover, indeed the latter is mentioned in the former, but they're not quite the same.<br /> <br /> (If they are meant to be different, I kinda feel they'd benefit from being swapped.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T09:32:56-07:00","id":1508897,"title":"","content":"The naked ambition and wish to reclaim Imperium for humanity probably ingratiated them with the Silver Ladder. The fact they get positive results makes mage society tolerate their ruthlessness. Meanwhile a deeply Hubristic philosophy and the seeds of their future infamy threaten to make them push too far. Its very well done, portraying their Order as a powder keg that will eventually explode.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T09:57:54-07:00","id":1508899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508893#post1508893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although it raises the question that it's still a rewrite, it <i>is</i> different. Are we meant to take away that the Tremere have meaningfully changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't bring the new text right in front of me for the moment, but putting the best I can recall of it against the Night Horrors write-up, I find a notable distinction between the original idea of Hunger primarily in a more abstract form of an actively pursued and cultivated ambition, a sense that enlightenment is there for the taking and must be yearned for without reservation, and the version of the Order in which all are Hollow and the Hunger is a much more literal thing of &quot;you have converted yourself into a void through which the vitality of souls can be fed as sustenance for the Seventh Dragon&quot;. Indeed, there's quite an emphasis in the write-up for the modern Tremere that they escew the abstract in many regards, that they place a greater value in the lived experience, the direct action. I think that's a foundation for why they view themselves as superior to the rest, that their philosophy expresses itself very directly upon their physical and metaphysical forms compared to other Orders who might be regarded as applying their philosophies as more aspirational or allegorical.<br /> <br /> That, I think, would be why the shift in magical symbolism works. The former is for when most Tremere are experiencing Hunger as an idea, the latter for when that gaping is experienced bone deep in a fashion that is considered most revelatory and validating to their ideas about the relationship between subtle and gross. A tenth century Tremere might leave their yearning alone for a while with no ill effect, but a modern one viscerally carries it with them every single day.<br /> <br /> So I see these things and I do indeed believe that there's a transition that runs deeper than just &quot;they're all Hollow now and don't align with the Diamond sect&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T10:03:18-07:00","id":1508902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508897#post1508897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...portraying their Order as a powder keg that will eventually explode.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I read it, they've already long exploded. Like, the Tremere have already gone through the Captivity and become Hollowed.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T10:03:57-07:00","id":1508903,"title":"","content":"From write-up, I do not understand them and their place in Medieval Diamond. Tremere here sound as from start corrupted Silver Ladders or (future) Mysterium. I really do not understand WHY Diamond wanted them so badly in alliance. ( Beside adding whole Dragon imaginary to Orders. \ud83e\udd37)<br /> <br /> BTW: Do we have date when Tremere were expelled from Diamond alliance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T11:01:00-07:00","id":1508911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508903#post1508903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not understand them and their place in Medieval Diamond.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, there may well be more information about the Diamond in the Medieval era that we just don't have yet. Still, they seem to be monster hunters. I guess the idea is that they fill a bit of the Arrow's niche, but maybe more proactive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really do not understand WHY Diamond wanted them so badly in alliance. </div> </div> </div>They didn't:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Order now known as Tremere formally \u2014 and aggressively \u2014 requested Diamond membership. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BTW: Do we have date when Tremere were expelled from Diamond alliance? </div> </div> </div><i>Nameless &amp; Accursed</i> gives a date of around 1100 CE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T12:35:18-07:00","id":1508916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508902#post1508902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I read it, they've already long exploded. Like, the Tremere have already gone through the Captivity and become Hollowed.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It would appear from the write-up, combined with Dave's comments in the last preview thread, that at this point those who are Hollowed are like a secret conspiracy at the heart of the Order. Even then, it's never the basis of why they are fully expelled from the Diamond; that was from the recognition that they were assimilating other Reaper Legacies, rather than destroying them outright. It seems as though the rest of the Diamond never fully recognised what they were dealing with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T13:32:23-07:00","id":1508922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508916#post1508916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would appear from the write-up, combined with Dave's comments in the last preview thread, that at this point those who are Hollowed are like a secret conspiracy at the heart of the Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but my point is it's already happened. The point of no return has already been crossed, it's simply a matter of how long it takes the Diamond to notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T16:08:07-07:00","id":1508934,"title":"","content":"I still do not get WHY Diamond embraced Tremere in this 8th century. 'Hi, you MUST take us in. RIGHT NOW. We have chantries all over the world., We TOTALLY not devour souls and killing Bound in the Fallen World. They just sorta disappear around us *wink-wink* Your Adamantine Arrows are just us, only weaker.'<br /> <br /> I just cannot fanthom Diamond Masters just did not say:'Riiiggghhhtt... And you really are not Exarchs cat's paws? Riiiggghhhtt...'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T16:26:25-07:00","id":1508937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508903#post1508903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From write-up, I do not understand them and their place in Medieval Diamond. Tremere here sound as from start corrupted Silver Ladders or (future) Mysterium. I really do not understand WHY Diamond wanted them so badly in alliance. ( Beside adding whole Dragon imaginary to Orders. \ud83e\udd37)<br /> <br /> BTW: Do we have date when Tremere were expelled from Diamond alliance?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the continued usage of the Dragon symbology wasn't already a tip off, the short answer is &quot;they brought increased knowledge of magic and implementations thereof to the Diamond, and even after their explusion, their inclusion had a marked benefit to the Diamond.&quot;<br /> <br /> In some of the specifics, the Tremere are explicitly spelled out as the most concerned (in their time) in the mysteries of the soul and the mastery of the Subtle Arcana, intent on utilizing the lot as the whole fruit for cider as opposed to a more sliced up version for juice (as it were), and tackled the harshest ends of getting wisdom and secrets from gods and monsters. Their ambition and dedication to shaking the boundaries challenged what was at that point more than a millenia worth of established traditions, which was useful running all the practices and ideologies of the Diamond through Chestertons' Fence.<br /> <br /> In an era where humanism had yet to come into formal philosophy, the Tremere undoubtedly sowed the seeds for the future shape of the Silver Ladder (and by extension the Free Council) by emphasizing the power and right of humanity to grasp, wield and consume magic as opposed to being inclined towards systems of intercession. Their interest in the unification of the soul and the effects of the Watchtowers upon wizards, for better and for worse, would supplement and bolster the Alethian traditions of the Guardians of the Veil, and also uncomfortably the secret center of the Tremere would be a valuable set of lessons learned by the Guardians in terms of their Esoteric Tenets and the practices emergent from them. THe Adamantine Arrows would likewise gain valuable insight into warefare-as-magical-enlightment from their god and monster hunting ways, and the Mysterium are arguably only a phrasing of precept away from <i>being</i> Tremere.<br /> <br /> And of course, the Tremere brought in the draconic symbolism that has come to be a significant form of each Order's Shadow Name since then. None of this is a small thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508922#post1508922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but my point is it's already happened. The point of no return has already been crossed, it's simply a matter of how long it takes the Diamond to notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tome of the Pentacle is there to explore, among other things, the history of the Orders of the Pentacle Alliance and how they ended up the way they are today. The Tremere's public facing Order contributed a lot to the shape of the modern day Diamond in terms of just sheer contribution , both from what the orders took positively from their inclusion and the ways that the various orders filled in the hole with the Tremere's expulsion-it wasn't that long ago you brought it to our attention that the Silver Ladder did have ambitions against vampires, and that probably has it's roots in the way the Tremere helped them define their relationship to monsters and in taking on the role of paternal humanist priests, as mentioned above.<br /> <br /> It's also significant because the betrayal of the Tremere has left wounds on the Diamond that persist to the modern day as taboos, particularly as deep study of the soul goes and ambitious exploitations of gods and other supernaturals go.<br /> <br /> And finally, it's important to understand how the Tremere themselves evolved. Arguably, if the Tremere never joined the DIamond and then suffered a civil war, the Tremere would likely be operating (more) openly (I don't think they'd ever be out and out open) as a major Sect of magic. The ability to reliably manipulate the other orders is also a likely reason why some of the Major Houses grew to the prominence they did in the wake of the expulsion.<br /> <br /> The Tremere, alongside the Keepers of the Word and the Pancryptiates, had an impact on the Diamond, and even the Pentacle Alliance, that lasts into the modern day of wizardry. Understanding that history not only helps to fill out the setting, it also sets up story seeds for yonks and even suggests tools that players can explore and pick up that might not be obvious if you just take the modern Pentacle ALliance's word for everything.<br /> <br /> The past is <i>power</i>, in a setting where <i>power is the point</i>. Why <i>would </i>this be ignored?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-19-2023, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T16:29:28-07:00","id":1508938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508934#post1508934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still do not get WHY Diamond embraced Tremere in this 8th century. 'Hi, you MUST take us in. RIGHT NOW. We have chantries all over the world., We TOTALLY not devour souls and killing Bound in the Fallen World. They just sorta disappear around us *wink-wink* Your Adamantine Arrows are just us, only weaker.'<br /> <br /> I just cannot fanthom Diamond Masters just did not say:'Riiiggghhhtt... And you really are not Exarchs cat's paws? Riiiggghhhtt...'</div> </div> </div> </div>They explictly weren't Exarch's cat's paws, they had cool shit, and like the Guardians (and Pancryptiates of the time), they were <i>really good</i> at making their more private mythos very private. They proved a valuable ally, until they didn't . THis isn't complicated.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It should also be noted that your sneering portrayal of the affair betrays the fact you're approaching this with you out of character knowledge that the Tremere are bad guys and clearly not think about about how the Tremere and Diamond interactions went, including the fact that at this time, a grand majority of the Tremere were just wizards and their extended cults. They may have been dark and edgy, but no more so than the Guardians and Pancryptiayes of the time.<br /> <br /> More likely, a hyperbolic pitch that's still believable is &quot;Hey, you all have impressive resources and knowledge at your disposal, and we think we could learn a lot by adding our knowledge and resources to yours. Together, we could reach way further than either of us could do alone, particularly as we find out what 's getting in each of our ways and surpassing it. What'cha think?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-19-2023, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T16:34:47-07:00","id":1508939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508922#post1508922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but my point is it's already happened. The point of no return has already been crossed, it's simply a matter of how long it takes the Diamond to notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think for Kaiser it's the noticing that constitutes the actual explosion, the upheaval around an entire Order being expelled from the Diamond. Finding the Seventh Dragon is more like lighting the fuse.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508934#post1508934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still do not get WHY Diamond embraced Tremere in this 8th century. 'Hi, you MUST take us in. RIGHT NOW. We have chantries all over the world., We TOTALLY not devour souls and killing Bound in the Fallen World. They just sorta disappear around us *wink-wink* Your Adamantine Arrows are just us, only weaker.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the argument for entry into the Diamond would be some combination of presenting a compelling thesis for how they could fit into the Atlantean model, initially presenting a greater focus on the hunting of monsters and Reapers in a way that managed to appeal, and perhaps no small amount of bribery with compelling secrets that they had acquired through their methods.<br /> <br /> It should be considered that at this point in history, the Adamantine Arrow are not focused on being martial defenders of the Awakened; they primarily express their thesis through attaching themselves to the conflicts and causes of Sleepers. If the Awakened Nation is concerned with being safeguarded from monsters and active destruction of Reapers, there's a niche available for that.<br /> <br /> As far as their crimes not being known yet, like... I'd presume the Tremere hid them. People conceal their crimes, it's not some massive leap that it took time and a greater degree of exposure and scrutiny for anybody to collect the data to form a more thorough picture of what the Tremere were actually about. If some Bound goes missing, there isn't an Amber Alert to notify every mage in the vicinity immediately.<br /> <br /> And I'd say for souls they could very well be doing what is the norm for modern Tremere, i.e. &quot;they don't consume those things to non-existence, they swap out ragged souls for fresh ones for the sake of discretion and sustainability&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just cannot fanthom Diamond Masters just did not say:'Riiiggghhhtt... And you really are not Exarchs cat's paws? Riiiggghhhtt...'</div> </div> </div> </div>It's canon that at this point in time there is no Seers of the Throne as a whole, and it's my personal inference that the Diamond understanding of the Exarchs is a lot less developed. Like, it's only a few hundred years into them really being proper Diamond Orders at all. I have a personal notion that it's actually a lot of the lore that gets brought in by the Tremere, their studies of Awakening and the soul, that begins to really help codify a full idea of what the Exarchs are (and it's not until the rise of the Church of Paternoster that there starts being a coherent idea that the Exarchs actually have mastery of the world).<br /> <br /> I would think the obstacle for Tremere isn't being regarded as cultists of the Exarchs*, it's the fact that they're Nameless, and the passage already provides the basics of how they might have gone about convincing others that they ought not to be.<br /> <br /> * Which I think, even if that was the concern, can be readily disproven by how adamant they are that all forms of divinity should be enslaved to humans, which I think can often be a hard position for Prelates to fake.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T17:14:11-07:00","id":1508941,"title":"","content":"Like, for clarity, the medieval Tremere aren't mostly a crowd of poorly concealed cackling <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vecna#:~:text=Vecna%20%28%20%2F%20%CB%88v%C9%9Bk.n%C9%91%CB%90%20%2F%20VEK-nah%20%5B2%5D%29%20is,a%20powerful%20wizard%20who%20became%20a%20lich.%20%5B4%5D\" target=\"_blank\">Vecna</a> wannabes, they're mostly <a href=\"https://dresdenfiles.fandom.com/wiki/Harry_Dresden\" target=\"_blank\">Harry Dresden</a>-as-<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Witcher\" target=\"_blank\">Witchers</a> with a morally neutral Slytherin bent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-19-2023, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T20:06:53-07:00","id":1508977,"title":"","content":"I think it was interesting how the Tremere glorify their past of slaying gods for the sake of humanity's Imperium and ripping their souls out for power and enlightenment, but now modern Tremere sacrifice their own souls and selfhood to a god (the Seventh Dragon) and prey on the souls of defenseless Sleepers in order to avoid death. It's quite the fall they went through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27614-phillip-morin","name":"Phillip Morin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27614_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T20:33:42-07:00","id":1508983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phillip Morin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508977#post1508977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was interesting how the Tremere glorify their past of slaying gods for the sake of humanity's Imperium and ripping their souls out for power and enlightenment, but now modern Tremere sacrifice their own souls and selfhood to a god (the Seventh Dragon) and prey on the souls of defenseless Sleepers in order to avoid death. It's quite the fall they went through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well now we have to play the other direction-it's not like there weren't any Tremere sacrificing their soul to the Seventh Watchtower, and it's not like they were interested in humanity-or, well, they are, but in so far as they are concerned with the one collected whole, true soul. The Hollow Tremere are and have always been the true core of the Tremere.<br /> <br /> But there's a value in good PR, and it's not like there's actually a contradiction between the two-just pieces that need to be put in place for the full picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T03:33:12-07:00","id":1509018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phillip Morin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1508768-tome-of-the-pentacle-the-tremere?p=1508977#post1508977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> modern Tremere sacrifice their own souls and selfhood to a god (the Seventh Dragon) and prey on the souls of defenseless Sleepers in order to avoid death.</div> </div> </div> </div>My read is that for the Tremere, the immortality is almost incidental, worth considering only insofar as it demonstrates the superiority of their state of existence. It's not about avoiding death, it's about living the ideal of magic hungering, with death as the incentive and punishment for failure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T10:31:25-07:00","id":1509060,"title":"","content":"^that, it's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}